.TH LLAPI_MIRROR_EXTEND 3 2026-11-23 "Lustre User API" "Lustre Library Functions"
.SH NAME
llapi_mirror_extend \- add a stale mirror to an existing file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
.PP
.BI "int llapi_mirror_extend(int " fd ", const struct llapi_layout *" layout );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add the components of
.I layout
to the file open on
.I fd
as one new mirror.
The new mirror is stale, and has no OST objects yet.
A plain file becomes a mirrored file with two mirrors.
.PP
The MDT allocates the objects of the new mirror when it is resynced, for
example with
.BR llapi_mirror_resync_many (3)
or
.BR lfs-mirror-resync (1),
and places them on other OSTs than the overlapping components of the
other mirrors of the file.
A parity component of
.I layout
protects the data mirror named by its link id, as set by
.BR llapi_layout_comp_add_parity_only (3).
.PP
The mirror count and the FLR state of
.I layout
are ignored.
The layout cached by the client is refreshed after the mirror is added
with a lease, so a following
.BR llapi_layout_get_by_fd (3)
returns the new mirror, unless the file is open for write or leased
elsewhere.
.SH RETURN VALUES
Return 0 on success, or a negative errno on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
.B EINVAL
.I layout
is not a valid composite layout of one mirror, its DoM component has
another size than that of the file, a parity component does not
match a data component of the file, or every mirror of the file is
stale.
.TP
.B EEXIST
A data component is already protected by a parity component.
.TP
.B EOPNOTSUPP
The MDT cannot add a mirror in place,
.I layout
has a parity component and erasure coding is disabled on the client, or
.I layout
names the OSTs of a component or has an extension, foreign or released
component, which only a mirror copied into a new file keeps, or the file
is released by HSM,
which reading the data to copy it restores, is cached by PCC-RO, or has
a resync that did not complete.
The caller can copy the data into a new file and merge its layout into
the file instead, as
.BR lfs-mirror-extend (1)
does.
.TP
.B ENODATA
The file has no layout yet.
.TP
.B EPERM
The caller does not own the file and does not have
.BR CAP_FOWNER ,
or the file is immutable or append-only.
.TP
.B ERANGE
The file already has the maximum number of mirrors.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add a mirror of one 4-stripe component to the file
.IR path ,
then copy the data of the file into it with
.BR lfs-mirror-resync (1):
.EX
        struct llapi_layout *layout;
        int fd, rc;
\&
        fd = open(path, O_RDONLY);
        if (fd < 0)
                /* error, errno is set */
\&
        layout = llapi_layout_alloc();
        if (layout == NULL)
                /* error, out of memory */
\&
        /* one component, so that the layout is composite */
        if (llapi_layout_comp_extent_set(layout, 0, LUSTRE_EOF) < 0 ||
            llapi_layout_stripe_count_set(layout, 4) < 0)
                rc = -errno;
        else
                rc = llapi_mirror_extend(fd, layout);
        llapi_layout_free(layout);
        close(fd);
        if (rc == -EOPNOTSUPP)
                return copy_and_merge(path);    /* as lfs-mirror-extend does */
        if (rc != 0)
                return rc;      /* the file is unchanged */
\&
        execlp("lfs", "lfs", "mirror", "resync", path, NULL);
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llapi_mirror_extend()
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
user application interface library since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_6x-xxx-gxxxxxxxxx
.SH SEE ALSO
